msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is our pleasure to announce the release of Quarkus 3.33, which is our new "
"LTS (Long Term Support) version."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This version is built on the top of Quarkus 3.32.\n"
"New features landed in https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-34-released/"
"[Quarkus 3.34], which was also released today."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you want to know more about our LTS policy, the https://quarkus.io/blog/"
"lts-releases/[LTS announcement] is a must read."
msgstr ""

msgid "LTS releases are supported for 12 months."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are coming from the previous LTS, Quarkus 3.27 LTS, there are a lot "
"of exciting new features and we recommend reading the following "
"announcements:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-28-released/[Quarkus 3.28 - More security "
"features, custom Grafana dashboards, support for multiple clients in "
"Liquibase MongoDB, and more]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-29-released/[Quarkus 3.29 - Multiple cache "
"backends and Qute DAP debugger support]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-30-released/[Quarkus 3.30 - JsonView on "
"REST Client, Hibernate Validator 9.1, CLI decrypt command, and more]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-31-released/[Quarkus 3.31 - Full Java 25 "
"support, Quarkus Maven packaging, Panache Next, and more!]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-32-released/[Quarkus 3.32 - Project Leyden "
"integration, more graceful shutdown, automatic Consul registration and "
"more!]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To update to Quarkus 3.33 LTS, we recommend updating to the latest version "
"of the Quarkus CLI and run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that `quarkus update` can update your applications from any version of "
"Quarkus (including 2.x) to Quarkus 3.33 LTS."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are upgrading from 3.32, there's nothing to do as 3.33 LTS is the "
"direct continuation of 3.32."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are upgrading from the previous LTS, Quarkus 3.27 LTS, please refer "
"to the following migration guides:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.28[Migration "
"guide for 3.28]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.29[Migration "
"guide for 3.29]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.30[Migration "
"guide for 3.30]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.31[Migration "
"guide for 3.31]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.32[Migration "
"guide for 3.32]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.33[Migration "
"guide for 3.33] - this one is empty as 3.33 is the continuation of 3.32"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that `quarkus update` should handle most of the heavy lifting for you,\n"
"but there are still cases that should be handled manually and we recommend "
"reading these migration guides carefully."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Platform component upgrades"
msgstr ""

